      "title": "Learning at the Cycle Workshop",
      "text": "When Lina’s old bicycle began making a clicking sound, she took it to the small cycle workshop near her apartment. The owner, Mr Doran, fixed the problem quickly, but Lina stayed to watch. He explained that the chain had become dry and showed her how to clean it with a brush. Lina asked if she could help at the workshop on Saturdays. Mr Doran agreed, as long as she arrived on time and listened carefully.\n\nDuring her first week, Lina pumped tyres and organised tools. Later, she learned to tighten a loose brake cable. Her hands were often dirty, and she sometimes needed several tries to fit a wheel correctly. Still, Mr Doran told her that careful work mattered more than speed. Lina kept a small notebook where she drew simple pictures of each repair.\n\nAfter two months, Lina repaired her neighbour’s bicycle without help. The neighbour offered to pay her, but Lina asked for a packet of seeds instead. She planned to grow flowers beside the workshop door. For Lina, the workshop had become more than a place to solve a problem; it was a place where she could build useful skills and help others travel safely.",
      "table": null
    },
